Hi,=0A=
=0A=
My company has also started having what appears to be the same problem, sin=
ce we upgraded our embedded system to =0A=
linux kernel 3.16.=0A=
=0A=
I tried applying the suggested fix of READ_ONCE (and also had to add in the=
 necessary code to compiler.h as 3.16=0A=
didn't have it) and unfortunately it did not fix the issue at all.=0A=
=0A=
Unfortunately we do not have an easy reproduction method, and do not know p=
recisely what is going on in the system=0A=
when the issue occurs. We know it is a multicast UDP packet but that is abo=
ut it. For us, the crash happens during=0A=
a critical stage in our system initialisation, making additional debugging =
and instrumentation difficult. Our =0A=
reproduction rate is approximately 1 out of 100 test runs; testing overnigh=
t we will usually see 3-5 instances of =0A=
the crash happening. All our attempts to increase the reproduction rate, or=
 reproduce the issue in a simpler/more =0A=
controlled way have failed.=0A=
=0A=
Because we have customised the linux kernel, in some places radically, we a=
ssumed this was just a problem only we =0A=
were seeing, so we were trying to fix it ourselves. Now that this appears t=
o be a generic problem upstream, we've =0A=
simply disabled UDP early demux in our system (since it's a new optimisatio=
n that we have lived without up till =0A=
now) and will wait for this issue to be fixed upstream instead.=0A=
=0A=
=0A=
So I'm sharing the debug patch I've written to help gather data on what is =
going on in the system, and some=0A=
of the output we've gotten from the debug, in case this is useful for anyon=
e else who is seeing this problem or=0A=
would like to try and fix it.=0A=
=0A=
Feel free to ask questions, I'm not sure how much help I can be but will do=
 my best. We'll be happy to assist in=0A=
testing any proposed fixes. I also have some more examples of kernel oops a=
nd debug output if that could be useful, =0A=
although the debug is from earlier iterations of the patch so that historic=
al output is not as detailed as the =0A=
output generated by the latest version of the patch attached here.=0A=
=0A=
Thanks,=0A=
Greg Hoggarth=

